hadiths[72]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6983","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the son of Adam (man), and this is his death, and there is his hope, and there is his hope, and there is his hope."""
"6984","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is hope, and this is his death; so while he is in this state, suddenly the nearest line comes to him."""
"6985","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is man, and this line surrounding him is his death, and this line that extends outside is his hope, and these small lines are afflictions; so if this one misses him, that one strikes him, and if that one misses him, this one strikes him."""
"6986","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is gourd; we increase our food with it."""
"6987","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the one for whom the Throne shook, for whom the gates of the heavens were opened, and at whose funeral seventy thousand angels were present; he was squeezed once, then that tightness was removed from him."""
"6988","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the place of standing, and the whole of Arafah is a place of standing."""
"6989","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the manner of ablution (wudu); so whoever does more than this has done wrong, or has transgressed and done injustice."""
"6990","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the time when knowledge will be snatched away from the people until they will not be able to obtain anything of it. O Ziyad! May your mother be bereaved of you! I used to count you among the jurists of the people of Madinah. These are the Torah and the Gospel with the Jews and the Christians, so of what benefit are they to them?!"""
"6991","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is Jibril (peace be upon him), holding the reins of his horse, with the equipment of war upon him."""
"6992","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is a mountain that loves us and we love it."""
"6993","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is a stone that was thrown into Hell seventy years ago, and it has been falling in Hell until now, when it has just reached its bottom."""
"6994","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is my maternal uncle; let any man show me his maternal uncle."""
"6995","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This month of Ramadan has come to you. In it the gates of Paradise are opened, in it the gates of Hell are closed, and in it the devils are chained."""
"6996","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is Quzah, and this is the place of standing, and the whole of Muzdalifah is a place of standing. I have sacrificed here, and the whole of Mina is a place of sacrifice, so sacrifice at your own campsites."""
"6997","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is Quzah, and this is the place of standing; the whole of Muzdalifah is a place of standing. This is the place of sacrifice, and the whole of Mina is a place of sacrifice."""
"6998","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This one (Talhah) is among those who have fulfilled their vow."""
"6999","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This one (Hasan) is from me, and Husayn is from Ali."""
"7000","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the place of the lower garment. If you wish to lower it further, then lower it further; and if you wish to lower it even beyond that, then know that the lower garment has no right below the ankles."""
"7001","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the One in whose Hand is my soul! This is among the blessings about which you will be questioned: cool shade, fresh good dates, and cool water."""
"7002","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the day of Ashura. Allah has not made its fast obligatory upon you, and I am fasting. So whoever wishes may fast, and whoever wishes may leave it."""
"7003","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These two are my sons and the sons of my daughter. O Allah, I love them both, so love them and love whoever loves them."""
"7004","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These two (Abu Bakr and Umar) are my hearing and sight."""
"7005","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These two (Abu Bakr and Umar) are the chiefs of the mature people of Paradise, from the first and the last, except for the Prophets and the Messengers. O Ali, do not tell them this."""
"7006","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This fire is one part out of a hundred parts of the fire of Hell."""
"7007","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is in return for that earlier race."""
"7008","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This (Hajj), and after it, (keep to) the backs of the mats (that is, remain in your homes)."""
"7009","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is mercy which Allah places in the hearts of whomever He wills among His servants, and Allah shows mercy only to those of His servants who are merciful."""
"7010","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the prayer of the homes (that is, the voluntary prayer after Maghrib)."""
"7011","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is Tabah (Madinah) and this is Uhud; it is a mountain that loves us and we love it."""
"7012","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is Arafah, and this is the place of standing, and the whole plain of Arafah is a place of standing."""
"7013","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is an Umrah by which we have performed tamattu'. So whoever does not have a sacrificial animal (hady) with him, let him come out of ihram completely, for Umrah has entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection."""
"7014","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This and this (the little finger and the thumb) are equal."""
"7015","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is how ablution (wudu) is. So whoever does more than this has done wrong and transgressed."""
"7016","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do it like this, for seeking permission is only to avoid looking into others' homes."""
"7017","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is there anyone here from such-and-such a tribe? Indeed, your companion is held back because of his debt."""
"7018","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Here is the land of trials, from where the horn of Satan rises."""
"7019","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Hassan satirised them, so he brought relief to the hearts (of the believers) and found relief himself."""
"7020","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A Muslim's cutting off his brother is like shedding his blood."""
"7021","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Gifts given to officials are misappropriated property."""
"7022","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mut'ah has been abolished by marriage, divorce, the waiting period ('iddah) and inheritance."""
"7023","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You are nothing but a finger that has bled, and what you have suffered is in the path of Allah."""
"7024","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Will you leave my commanders to me? The clear part of their affair is for you, and its murky part is upon them."""
"7025","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Will you leave my commanders to me? The example of you and them is like a man who was given camels or sheep to graze. He grazed them, then when the time came to water them, he brought them to a trough. They went into it, drank its clear water and left its murky water. So its clear part is for you and its murky part is upon them."""
"7026","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know where this (sun) sets? It sets in a hot spring."""
"7027","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what al-Kawthar is? It is a river which my Lord has given me in Paradise. There is abundant good in it. My Ummah will come to it on the Day of Resurrection. Its vessels are as numerous as the stars. A servant among them will suddenly be pulled away, and I will say: 'O Lord, he is from my Ummah!' And it will be said: 'You do not know what they innovated after you.'"""
"7028","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what your Lord said last night? Allah Almighty said: 'Some of My servants have entered the morning as believers in Me and some as disbelievers. Whoever said: We have been given rain by the grace of Allah and His mercy, that one is a believer in Me and a disbeliever in the stars. And whoever said: We have been given rain because of such-and-such a star, that one is a disbeliever in Me and a believer in the stars.'"""
"7029","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you see that my qiblah is only here in front of me? By Allah! Neither your humility nor your bowing is hidden from me; I see you even from behind my back."""
"7030","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you see what I see? Indeed, I see the places where trials will fall among your houses, like the places where raindrops fall."""
"7031","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you have any difficulty in seeing the sun at midday, when the sky is clear and there is no cloud over it? And do you have any difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon, when the sky is clear and there is no cloud over it? You will have no more difficulty in seeing Allah on the Day of Resurrection than you have in seeing either of them. When the Day of Resurrection comes, a caller will announce: 'Let every nation follow what it used to worship.' Then not one of those who worshipped idols and stone altars besides Allah will remain, except that they will fall into the Fire, until none remain except those who used to worship Allah, whether righteous or sinful, and some of the People of the Book. Then the Jews will be called and it will be said to them: 'What did you use to worship?' They will say: 'We used to worship Uzayr, the son of Allah!' It will be said: 'You have lied; Allah has taken neither a wife nor a son. What do you want?' They will say: 'O our Lord, we are thirsty, so give us water.' It will be pointed out to them: 'Will you not go there?' So they will be driven towards Hell, which will appear like a mirage, and they will fall into Hell crushing one another. Then the Christians will be called and it will be said to them: 'What did you use to worship?' They will say: 'We used to worship the Messiah, the son of Allah!' It will be said to them: 'You have lied; Allah has taken neither a wife nor a son.' It will be said to them: 'What do you want?' They will say: 'O our Lord, we are thirsty, so give us water.' It will be pointed out to them: 'Will you not go?' So they will be driven towards Hell, which will appear like a mirage, and they will fall into Hell crushing one another, until none remain except those who used to worship Allah, whether righteous or sinful. Then the Lord of the worlds will come to them in a form different from the one in which they had seen Him before, and He will say: 'What are you waiting for now? Let every nation follow what it used to worship.' They will say: 'O our Lord, in the world we parted from people at the time we needed them most, and we did not keep company with them.' He will say: 'I am your Lord.' They will say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from you; we will not associate anything with Allah,' saying this two or three times, until some of them will be close to turning back from faith. He will say: 'Is there a sign between you and Him by which you would recognise Him?' They will say: 'Yes, the shin.' Then He will uncover His shin, and none who used to prostrate to Allah sincerely from his heart will remain except that Allah will permit him to prostrate; and whoever used to prostrate out of fear or to show off, Allah will make his back a single rigid plank, and whenever he tries to prostrate he will fall on the back of his neck. Then they will raise their heads, and He will have changed into the form in which they saw Him the first time, and He will say: 'I am your Lord.' They will say: 'You are our Lord.' Then the bridge will be laid over Hell and intercession will be permitted, and they will say: 'O Allah, grant safety, grant safety.' It was asked: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the bridge?' He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'A slippery place on which there are hooks and thorny things, and a thorny plant found in Najd called al-Sa'dan. The believers will pass over it like the blink of an eye, like lightning, like the wind, like birds, and like fine horses and riding animals. Some will escape safe and sound, some will be let go after being scratched, and some will be thrown headlong into Hell. Then, when the believers are saved from the Fire, by the One in whose Hand is my soul! None of you pleads with Allah more earnestly for obtaining his right than the believers will plead with Allah on the Day of Resurrection for their brothers who are in the Fire. They will say: O our Lord, they used to fast with us, pray and perform Hajj. It will be said to them: Bring out those whom you recognise. Their faces will be forbidden to the Fire, and they will bring out a great many people whom the Fire had burned up to the middle of their shins and up to their knees. They will say: O our Lord, not one of those You commanded us about remains in it. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: Go back, and whoever you find with good in his heart equal to the weight of a dinar, bring him out. So they will bring out a great many people. Then they will say: O our Lord, we have not left anyone of those You commanded us about. Then He will say: Go back, and whoever you find with good in his heart equal to the weight of half a dinar, bring him out. So they will bring out a great many people, then they will say: O our Lord, we have not left anyone of those You commanded us about. Then He will say: Go back, and whoever you find with good in his heart equal to the weight of a speck, bring him out. So they will bring out a great many people, then they will say: O our Lord, we have not left any good in it. Allah will say: The angels have interceded, the Prophets have interceded and the believers have interceded, and none remains but the Most Merciful of the merciful. Then He will take a handful from the Fire and bring out of it people who never did any good at all, and who have turned into charcoal. Then He will cast them into a river at the entrances of Paradise called the River of Life, and they will sprout as a seed sprouts in the silt carried by a flood. Do you not see that the plant on the shaded side of a stone or a tree is white, and that which is towards the sun is yellowish or greenish? So they will come out like pearls, with seals of identification on their necks. The people of Paradise will recognise them and say: These are those whom Allah has freed from the Fire, whom He admitted into Paradise without any deed that they did and without any good that they sent ahead. Then He will say: Enter Paradise; whatever you see is yours. They will say: O our Lord, You have given us what You have not given to anyone among the people of the world. He will say: I have for you something better than this. They will say: O our Lord, what could be better than this? He will say: My pleasure; I will never be displeased with you after this.'"""
"7032","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you have any difficulty in seeing the sun at midday, when there is no cloud? Do you have any difficulty in seeing the moon on the night of the full moon, when there is no cloud? By the One in whose Hand is my soul! You will have no more difficulty in seeing your Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, than you have in seeing either of them. Then the servant will be met, and Allah will say: 'O so-and-so, did I not honour you, make you a chief, get you married, subject horses and camels to you, and let you lead and live in ease?' He will say: 'Of course, O my Lord.' Allah will say: 'Did you think that you would meet Me?' He will say: 'No.' Allah will say: 'Then I will forget you just as you forgot Me.' Then the second will be met, and Allah will say to him too: 'O so-and-so, did I not honour you, make you a chief, get you married, subject horses and camels to you, and let you lead and live in ease?' He will say: 'Of course, O my Lord.' Allah will say: 'Did you think that you would meet Me?' He will say: 'No.' Allah will say: 'Then I will forget you just as you forgot Me.' Then the third will be met, and Allah will say the same to him. He will say: 'O my Lord, I believed in You, in Your Book and in Your Messengers; I prayed, fasted and gave charity,' and he will praise himself as much as he can. Allah will say: 'Very well, stay right here.' Then it will be said: 'Now We will send a witness against you,' and he will think to himself: 'Who is it that will testify against me?' Then a seal will be placed on his mouth, and it will be said to his thigh: 'Speak!' So his thigh, his flesh and his bones will testify to his deeds. That will be so that he cannot offer any excuse for himself, and that is the hypocrite with whom Allah is displeased."""
"7033","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you have any doubt about the moon on the night of the full moon when there is no cloud in front of it? Do you have any doubt about seeing the sun when there is no cloud in front of it? Indeed, you will see Him likewise. Allah Almighty will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection and will say: 'Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it.' So whoever used to worship the sun will follow the sun, whoever used to worship the moon will follow the moon, and whoever used to worship the false deities (taghut) will follow the false deities. And this Ummah will remain, with its hypocrites among it. Allah Almighty will come to them in a form other than the form they recognise, and He will say: 'I am your Lord.' They will say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from you. We will stay here until our Lord comes to us, and when He comes to us we will recognise Him.' Then Allah Almighty will come to them in the form they recognise, and He will say: 'I am your Lord.' They will say: 'You are our Lord,' and they will follow Him. The bridge will be laid across the middle of Hell, and I will be the first of the Messengers to cross it with his Ummah. On that day no one will speak except the Messengers, and the speech of the Messengers on that day will be: 'Allahumma sallim sallim' (O Allah, grant safety, grant safety). In Hell there will be hooks like the thorns of al-Sa'dan, except that no one knows the extent of their size except Allah. They will snatch people according to their deeds. Some of them will be destroyed because of their deeds, and some will be cut to pieces and then be saved. Then, when Allah has finished judging between the servants and wishes, out of His mercy, to bring out whomever He wills of the people of the Fire, He will command the angels to bring out of the Fire whoever did not associate anything with Allah and used to say 'La ilaha illallah' (there is no god worthy of worship except Allah). They will bring them out and will recognise them by the marks of prostration, for Allah has forbidden the Fire to consume the marks of prostration. So they will come out of the Fire burnt to charcoal, and the Water of Life will be poured over them, and they will sprout as a seed sprouts in the silt carried by a flood. Then Allah will finish judging between the servants, and one man will remain between Paradise and Hell; he will be the last of the people of the Fire to enter Paradise, with his face turned towards Hell. He will say: 'O my Lord, turn my face away from the Fire, for its smell has sickened me and its flame has scorched me.' Allah will say: 'If I do that for you, will you ask for anything else?' He will say: 'No, by Your might.' So he will give Allah whatever covenants and pledges He wills, and Allah will turn his face away from the Fire. Then, when he is turned towards Paradise and sees its splendour, he will remain silent for as long as Allah wills. Then he will say: 'O my Lord, bring me close to the gate of Paradise.' Allah will say: 'Did you not give covenants and pledges that you would not ask for anything other than what you had asked?' He will say: 'O my Lord, let me not become the most wretched of Your creation.' Allah will say: 'If I give you this, will you not ask for anything else?' He will say: 'No, by Your might! I will not ask You for anything other than this.' So he will give his Lord whatever covenants and pledges He wills, and He will bring him to the gate of Paradise. Then, when he reaches its gate and sees its splendour and the freshness and joy within it, he will remain silent for as long as Allah wills, then he will say: 'O my Lord, admit me into Paradise.' Allah will say: 'Woe to you, O son of Adam! How treacherous you are! Did you not give covenants and pledges that you would not ask for anything other than what you were given?' He will say: 'O my Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation.' So Allah will laugh at him, then permit him to enter Paradise. Allah will say: 'Make a wish.' So he will wish until, when his wishes are exhausted, Allah Almighty will say: 'Ask for such-and-such as well,' and his Lord will keep reminding him, until, when his wishes come to an end, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say: 'All of that is yours, and as much again along with it.'"""
"7034","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Are you helped by anyone other than your weak ones? It is through their supplication and their sincerity."""
"7035","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Are you helped and given provision by anyone other than your weak ones?"""
"7036","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Did any of you recite along with me just now? I say within myself: What is the matter with me that I am being contended with in reciting the Qur'an?!"""
"7037","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Is there a man among you who, when he comes to his wife, closes his door, draws his curtain, and conceals himself with the covering of Allah?"" The Companions said: ""Yes."" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then after that he sits and says: 'I did such-and-such, I did such-and-such.'"" They all fell silent. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) turned to the women and said: ""Does any of you speak of such things?"" They too fell silent. Then a young girl knelt on one of her knees and raised herself up so that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) could see her and hear what she said, and she said: ""O Messenger of Allah! The men speak of these things and the women speak of them too!"" He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what the likeness of that is? The likeness of that is only that of a female devil who met a male devil in the street and he fulfilled his need with her while the people were watching! Beware! The perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent and whose colour is not apparent, and the perfume of women is that whose colour is apparent and whose scent is not apparent. Beware! No man should go close to another man, nor any woman to another woman, except with a child or a parent."""
"7038","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The destruction of my Ummah will be at the hands of some young men of Quraysh."""
"7039","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Those who go beyond the limits in religion are destroyed."""
"7040","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Kisra has perished, and there will be no Kisra after him; and Caesar will surely perish, and there will be no Caesar after him; and their treasures will surely be spent in the path of Allah."""
"7041","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why did you not take its hide, tan it and make use of it? Only eating it has been made unlawful."""
"7042","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why did you not leave him (Ma'iz)? Perhaps he would have repented and Allah would have accepted his repentance."""
"7043","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Come to the blessed breakfast, that is, the pre-dawn meal (suhur)."""
"7044","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Come to a jihad in which there is no fighting: it is Hajj."""
"7045","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""These two (Hasan and Husayn) are my two sweet basils of this world."""
"7046","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By the Lord of the Ka'bah! They are the greatest losers. By the Lord of the Ka'bah! They are the greatest losers, that is, on the Day of Resurrection, those who have the most wealth, except the one who spends it among the servants of Allah like this and like this, and such people are few. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Any man who dies leaving behind goats, camels or cattle without having paid their zakah, they will come to him on the Day of Resurrection in their biggest and fattest state; they will trample him with their hooves and butt him with their horns until judgement is passed between the people. Every time the last of them has passed, the first of them will come back again."""
"7047","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This looking here and there in prayer is something that Satan snatches from the prayer of the servant."""
"7048","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The water of this sea is purifying, and its dead animals are also lawful."""
"7049","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He is entirely free; Allah has no partner."""
"7050","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is charity for her, and from her it is a gift for us."""
"7051","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""He (Abu Talib) is in a shallow part of the Fire, and were it not for me he would have been in the lowest level of Hell."""
"7052","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take it easy on yourself; I am not a king. I am only the son of a woman of Quraysh who used to eat dried meat."""
"7053","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Emigration (hijrah) is of two kinds: the emigration of the town-dweller and the emigration of the Bedouin. As for the Bedouin, he responds when he is called and obeys when he is commanded; and the emigration of the town-dweller is the greater of the two in trial and the greater of the two in reward."""
"7054","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A gift given to the ruler is misappropriated wealth."""
